# Auth flows that return through a deep link

OAuth sign-in, magic links, email confirmation and password reset all end in
the browser, which has to hand a link back to the app. `supabase_flutter`
listens for that link through `app_links`, exchanges it for a session, and
emits the result on `onAuthStateChange`. The app has to own a URL scheme, and
the Supabase project has to allow it.

Native sign-in with `signInWithIdToken` (Google, Apple and Facebook SDKs) and
email or phone codes verified with `verifyOTP` do not leave the app and need
none of this.

## Rules

- Pick one redirect URL of the form `<scheme>://<host>`, with a scheme unique
  to the app, usually the reverse domain:
  `com.example.myapp://login-callback`.
- Pass it as `redirectTo` or `emailRedirectTo` on every flow, except on web.
- Add it to the redirect URL allow list of the project, or the server falls
  back to the Site URL and the app never opens.
- Register the scheme on every platform the app ships to, and turn off
  Flutter's own deep link handling there, so `app_links` receives the link.
- React to the result in `onAuthStateChange`, not after the call that opened
  the browser: the call returns before the user finishes in the browser.
- Keep the default pkce flow.

## 1. Allow the redirect URL

- Hosted project: Dashboard, Authentication, URL Configuration, Redirect URLs.
  Add `com.example.myapp://login-callback`.
- Local stack: in `supabase/config.toml`:

  ```toml
  [auth]
  additional_redirect_urls = ["com.example.myapp://login-callback"]
  ```

For web, add the origin the app is served from, for example
`http://localhost:3000/**` during development.

## 2. Register the scheme

Android, in `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`, inside the
`<activity>` of `.MainActivity`:

```xml
<meta-data android:name="flutter_deeplinking_enabled" android:value="false" />

<intent-filter>
  <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
  <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
  <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
  <data android:scheme="com.example.myapp" android:host="login-callback" />
</intent-filter>
```

iOS, in `ios/Runner/Info.plist`, inside the top-level `<dict>`, and the same
in `macos/Runner/Info.plist` for macOS:

```xml
<key>FlutterDeepLinkingEnabled</key>
<false/>
<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
<array>
  <dict>
    <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
    <string>Editor</string>
    <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
    <array>
      <string>com.example.myapp</string>
    </array>
  </dict>
</array>
```

If the app already uses Flutter deep linking for its router, keep it and let
the router ignore the auth callback path instead of disabling it.

Windows and Linux need the scheme registered with the system, as described in
the [`app_links` documentation](https://pub.dev/packages/app_links). Web needs
no registration.

## 3. Start the flow

```dart file
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';
import 'package:supabase_flutter/supabase_flutter.dart';

const redirectUrl = 'com.example.myapp://login-callback';

Future<void> startAuthFlows(SupabaseClient supabase) async {
  await supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth(
    OAuthProvider.github,
    redirectTo: kIsWeb ? null : redirectUrl,
  );

  await supabase.auth.signInWithOtp(
    email: 'user@example.com',
    emailRedirectTo: kIsWeb ? null : redirectUrl,
  );

  await supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail(
    'user@example.com',
    redirectTo: kIsWeb ? null : redirectUrl,
  );
}
```

`signUp` takes `emailRedirectTo` for the confirmation email in the same way.
On web, `null` returns to the current page, which `supabase_flutter` picks the
session up from.

## 4. Handle the result

Listen once, early, for example in the root widget's `initState`:

```dart
final subscription = supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange.listen(
  (state) {
    switch (state) {
      case AuthInitialSession(:final session):
        // The session restored at startup, or null.
        print(session == null ? 'Show sign in' : 'Show home');
      case AuthSignedIn():
        // OAuth, magic link and email confirmation end here.
        print('Show home');
      case AuthPasswordRecovery():
        // A password reset link was opened: ask for the new password.
        print('Show new password form');
      case AuthSignedOut():
        print('Show sign in');
      case _:
    }
  },
  // A failed exchange, such as an expired link, or a token refresh that
  // failed while offline.
  onError: (Object error) => print('Auth error: $error'),
);
```

Finish a password reset with the new password:

```dart
await supabase.auth.updateUser(UserAttributes(password: 'a-new-password'));
```

A failed exchange, for example an expired link, arrives as an
`AuthException` error on the same stream, and so does a token refresh that
failed while the device was offline. Always pass `onError`: without it these
errors are unhandled and reach the zone's error handler.

## Sign out

`signOut()` removes the session from the device and emits `AuthSignedOut`
as soon as it is called, so it works offline. The returned future then waits
up to 10 seconds for the server to revoke the session, and throws an
`AuthException` when that fails. The user stays signed out on the device
either way.

To keep the button snappy, navigate right away and handle a failed revoke in
the background:

```dart
supabase.auth.signOut().onError<AuthException>(
  // Signed out on this device, but the session stays valid on the server
  // until it expires.
  (error, _) => print('Could not revoke the session: ${error.message}'),
);
// Navigate to the sign in screen here.
```

## When the app does not open, or opens without a session

| Symptom                                              | Cause and fix                                                                                                     |
| ---------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| The browser lands on the Site URL                    | The redirect URL is missing from the allow list, or differs from `redirectTo` in scheme, host or path.            |
| The browser shows the link but the app does not open | The scheme is not registered on that platform, or the intent filter is outside `.MainActivity`.                   |
| The app opens but no `AuthSignedIn` arrives          | Flutter deep linking is still enabled and consumed the link, or the listener was attached after the link came in. |
| The exchange fails with a missing code verifier      | The flow was started on another device or browser than it finished on. Start and finish on the same device.       |
| A link from an email works once, then fails          | Email links are single use and expire. Request a new one.                                                         |
